Letters to the Editor         NannyMUD Times                     Page 3

  +-=-+-=-+-=-+-=-+-=-+-=-+-=-+-=-+-=-+-=-+-=-+-=-+-=-+
  I for one am glad that the NannyMud Times has been
  put back into production. As it was said with your
  interview with Vulcan, NannyMud doesn't seem (sadly)
  the place where many new faces are found drinking in
  our favourite pubs anymore. But, for those of us who have
  been here and have no intention of leaving anytime soon,
  (hopefully), I believe that the NannyMud Times will make
  our community stronger. The player profiles are a great
  addition. Those of us who see eachother on an almost
  daily basis, going about our -own- adventures, may come
  to learn or understand eachother, find common interests,
  and really make this mud a more friendly and even
  diverse place to come and enjoy ourselves.
  
  I just wanted to let you know that I appreciate your
  efforts and I'm sure that many more share these
  sentiments. Thanks, Astrodeath.
  
  Trake, Paladin of Camelot.
  +-=-+-=-+-=-+-=-+-=-+-=-+-=-+-=-+-=-+-=-+-=-+-=-+-=-+
  
